    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347-a1">

                <pb facs="0788" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg774"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mondy, collector,
                        to Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacksonville, Florida</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Custom-House</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi>
                        26, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[34]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, in reply to your letter
                    of 22d instant, directing that I examine and report if there be any such vessel
                    fitting out in *this port, as Salvador or other, with intent of being a Cuban
                    privateer; &amp;c., to inform you that there is no steamer or other vessel in
                    this port fitting or preparing to fit out for any such object. There are no
                    steamers in this port, except our regular river-boats, besides the steam
                    pleasure-yacht Fire-Fly, of New York, belonging to Mr. T. P. James, who is on
                    board with his family.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P. MONDY, <hi rendition="#italic">Collector.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury, Washington, D.
                        C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
